      dealing: 'Each player is dealt 11 cards (in some variants 13). The remaining cards form the stock pile. One card is turned up to start the discard pile.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Draw**: On your turn, draw one card from the stock or take the top card from the discard pile. 2. **Melding**: You can lay down melds as soon as you have them. In the first round, you usually need a minimum 'opening' count (e.g., 30 or 40 points in some variants). 3. **Laying Off**: You can add cards to your own or opponents' existing melds on the table. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by discarding one card to the discard pile.",
