    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 11 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Form all cards in your hand into valid melds and 'go out' (empty your hand). Lowest cumulative score across all rounds wins.",
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Draw**: On your turn, draw one card from the stock or take the top card from the discard pile. 2. **Melding**: You can lay down melds as soon as you have them. In the first round, you usually need a minimum 'opening' count (e.g., 30 or 40 points in some variants). 3. **Laying Off**: You can add cards to your own or opponents' existing melds on the table. 4. **Discard**: End your turn by discarding one card to the discard pile.",
      'Scoring example: Penalty points for cards remaining in hand when another player goes out. Lowest cumulative score after agreed number of rounds or when a player reaches a penalty threshold (e.g., 200 points)..',
